    "attributes": {
      "name": "Makeway — Practical Boxel Tool Library",
      "summary": "# Makeway — a practical Boxel tool shelf\n\nMakeway is a Boxel workspace with a curated collection of focused utilities and a guided tool-library home. It includes a prompt brief builder, Markdown outline extractor, text cleaner, UTM builder, aspect-ratio calculator, QR value presenter, regex tester, CSV normalizer, and cURL-to-Fetch converter. Tools validate input and show their output in the workspace.\n\nThe Skills section can open workspace skills in the Boxel AI assistant. The experimental MCP connector supports browser-side HTTPS Streamable HTTP servers that need no authentication and allow CORS; it can list tools and invoke a selected tool with JSON arguments. It does not support local stdio servers, OAuth or API-key authentication, legacy SSE-only endpoints, or servers that deny browser access. Only connect to a server you trust; calls go directly from the browser to that server.\n\nBuilt as Boxel Cards and Commands with a responsive home view. No external service credentials are embedded. This listing does not promise persistent tool results, scheduled jobs, or arbitrary MCP execution.",
